PUBLISHED REVISION ARCHIVE
==========================

One zip per superseded revision of one document, named
<document id>__Revision__<letter>.zip - the whole document folder as it stood
when that revision was current.

A zip is made ONLY when the revision letter CHANGES. Re-publishing the same
revision overwrites the document folder in place and archives nothing, so an
unissued revision that is worked on all afternoon leaves one folder and no
zips, and an issued revision can never be lost.

The zip is written by the local server, not by the browser: Python's zipfile,
one call, and no zip library to vendor into the app.

THIS FOLDER IS LOCAL. It starts with 00__, and the R2 sync skips every folder
whose name starts with 00__ (SKIP_FOLDER_PREFIXES in
CloudflareR2__ModelSync__Main__.py), so no archive zip ever reaches the bucket,
the CDN or a client. Only the latest revision of each document is published.

A past revision is therefore recoverable on this machine and nowhere else. If
past revisions are ever wanted on the live site they go in a sibling folder
that does not start with 00__, and PublishedDocuments__Index__.json already has
a place to name them (PublishedDocuments__Superseded).
